{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I have cleared the sacred portion from the house.</b> Through our sins and the iniquities of our fathers the service was removed from the firstborn, to whom terumot and tithes were properly due, as it says: וָאֲטַמֵּא אוֹתָם בְּמַתְּנוֹתָם בְּהַעֲבִיר כָּל פֶּטֶר רֶחֶם (Ezekiel 20:26). This is the declaration of tithing that our Rabbis of blessed memory mentioned for blessing." "<b>And I have also given it to the Levite.</b> The sense of גַם is like אַף עַל פִּי, as in גַּם הָיִיתִי הַלַּיְלָה לְאִישׁ וְגַם יָלַדְתִּי בָּנִים (Ruth 1:12). He says accordingly: I acknowledge that my iniquity is great, for I caused the sacred portion to be cleared from the house; yet even though I gave it to the Levite and others according to Your command, I pray that You look upon me with a favorable regard in place of the unfavorable regard my iniquity warrants."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:18.918030856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}